commit ef79045c777d7a03f8df7d4ec48f177d4b00ec1d
Author: Michael Yankelev <myankelev@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Sep 26 03:31:23 2026 +0200

    fix(web): always offer the remove choice on a link revoke

    The engine shows a via-link tag and a name only on a row the owner
    attests. A link revoke with remove-grantees also takes a row the owner
    does not attest when its via-link names the link, or when a contact the
    link sourced holds its key. The dialog hid the choice and sent false
    when no visible row named the link, so those people kept access.

    The prompt now always shows the choice and sends it as the owner sets
    it. It still lists the people whose row names the link. It marks the
    list unclear only when a grant has no name and no link, because only
    such a row can hide a joiner.

